cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "dubforge: multi-provider AI video dubbing with a quality-controlled pipeline"
message: "If you use dubforge in research or teaching material, cite it like this."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Chaudhary"
    given-names: "Vivek"
    alias: "chaudharyvivek1"
    website: "https://github.com/chaudharyvivek1"
repository-code: "https://github.com/chaudharyvivek1/dubforge"
url: "https://github.com/chaudharyvivek1/dubforge"
license: MIT
version: "0.9.2"
date-released: "2026-11-18"
abstract: >-
  A dubbing pipeline that coordinates several AI providers: speech recognition with
  diarisation, duration-aware translation with a rewrite loop, per-speaker voice
  synthesis, stem separation to preserve music and effects, and a QC report with ten
  checks. Exposed as a Python library, a CLI, an MCP server and an agent skill.
keywords:
  - dubbing
  - audiovisual translation
  - text-to-speech
  - speech recognition
  - voice cloning
  - Indian languages
  - localisation
  - MCP
  - ffmpeg
